{"type":"match","data":{"path":{"text":"latinooutdoors.org/Our People.txt"},"lines":{"text":"Rouvaishyana was born and raised in Indiana and Michigan, then moved to California as an adult. Hiking at State Parks with his family as a child, he later became a California State Park Interpreter (naturalist), leading hundreds of guided programs, working with volunteers, cataloging natural history specimens, and giving astronomy programs. He has also worked for many years in the private whale and wildlife watching sector in Morro Bay, CA. There he realized how many people in California speak Spanish, so he began learning the language as an adult, in order to be more welcoming to the Latinoamerican community. He plans to help start a chapter of Latino Outdoors in San Luis Obispo county, and lead or co-lead outings. He is an active birder, and is currently learning the names of California birds in Spanish.\n"},"line_number":579,"absolute_offset":76655,"submatches":[{"match":{"text":"co-lead"},"start":709,"end":716}]}}
